#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""link-parity-harness — differential oracle for the `borg link` zsh->Python port.

WHAT THIS PROVES
-----------------
During the ship review for the `borg link` port (docs/plans/PROJECT_PLAN.md), a reviewer ran the
LAST zsh implementation of `borg link` (deleted in Phase 3) against the current Python port across
all real projects in the owner's registry. 9 of 20 projects differed, and EVERY difference was one
of three owner-signed-off deviations recorded in PROJECT_PLAN.md. That is the strongest evidence in
the whole plan that the port preserves behavior -- and it existed nowhere as a rerunnable artifact
until this script. The zsh renderers only exist in git history now, at commit ad99612 (the tree
immediately before the Phase 3 render flip, eb81eab~1) -- there is no other way to reproduce this
comparison once that commit falls out of anyone's local reflog expiry.

This script:
  1. Extracts the ad99612 tree (`git archive`) into a scratch dir and confirms it still contains
     the deleted renderers (_borg_link_porcelain, _borg_link_overview, _borg_link_deep).
  2. Runs all four human `borg link` modes (overview, --porcelain, --all, and a deep dive per
     project) through BOTH that tree's `borg.zsh` and the CURRENT tree's `borg.zsh` (which
     dispatches to borg_core.link via `_borg_py`), against an isolated copy of a registry.
  3. Normalizes relative-time text and the three known-expected deviations, then diffs what's left.
  4. Classifies every remaining difference as EXPECTED (matches one of the three deviations below)
     or UNEXPECTED. An unexpected difference is the entire point of this tool -- it means the port
     drifted from the oracle in some way nobody signed off on.

It also runs (via `primitives`) differentials of the individual ported primitives against the exact
shell one-liners they replace: core.heading_title, core.ship_date, core.plan_progress,
core.plan_objective. `render._fold_s` vs `fold -s` is already covered by
`test_matches_real_fold_s_binary` in borg_core/link/test_render.py -- NOT duplicated here.

THE THREE EXPECTED DEVIATIONS (all owner-signed-off, PROJECT_PLAN.md)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
  1. `(NOm)` assimilated ordering -- zsh's per-project deep dive lists the three OLDEST assimilated
     plans (`_borg_read_assimilated`'s glob reverses to oldest-first); Python lists newest-first.
     Only the ORDER of the "Recently assimilated:" bullet block differs; the same lines are present
     on both sides. Detected by sorting that block on both sides and comparing.
  2. The empty `Progress: 0` / `0/N criteria met` two-line artifact -- zsh's
     `criteria_done=$(grep -c '^- [x]' ... || echo 0)` captures BOTH grep's own printed "0" (grep
     exits 1 but still prints a count) and the `|| echo 0` fallback, so `$criteria_done` becomes the
     two-line string "0\n0" and the single `echo -e "Progress: $criteria_done/$criteria_total..."`
     splits across two lines whenever nothing is checked off. Python renders one line.
  3. The empty-`Shipped:` field-shift -- zsh's aggregate overview reads a TSV row with
     `IFS=$'\t' read -r slug title ship_date aproject`. Tab is an IFS whitespace character, so zsh
     COLLAPSES a run of tabs when a field (ship_date) is empty, shifting `aproject`'s value into
     `ship_date`'s slot and leaving `aproject` empty. The render becomes
     `- [] <title> (<project>)` instead of `- [<project>] <title>`. Python's port already renders
     the corrected shape and omits the parens entirely when ship_date is empty (this was found
     POST-MERGE against the real registry, is a fix not a regression, and is why "9 of 20 differ" is
     the expected steady-state count, not zero).

Anything that survives normalization is printed as a unified diff and marked UNEXPECTED, and the
script exits non-zero.

SANDBOX GOTCHAS BAKED IN (rediscover these once, never again)
-----------------------------------------------------------------
  - `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` must be overridden, not just `BORG_REGISTRY`. `borg.zsh:24` and
    `lib/registry.zsh:14-15` recompute `BORG_DIR`/`BORG_REGISTRY` from `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` on every
    invocation, so exporting `BORG_REGISTRY` alone is silently ignored and every command falls
    through to the REAL registry. This script only ever sets `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` to a throwaway temp
    dir and copies the registry snapshot into `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/borg/registry.json` -- it never
    writes to `~/.config/borg/registry.json`. The snapshot is re-copied fresh before every single
    invocation so `borg_desktop_scan`'s registry merge (a real side effect on the overview/porcelain
    paths) can never leak state from one comparison into the next.
  - `BORG_NO_REAP=1` is set for every child. Without it, the reap overlay's status downgrades depend
    on wall-clock time and live tmux window state, making two runs of the SAME implementation
    disagree.
  - Relative-time text ("3m ago" vs "1m ago") differs between two runs of the identical
    implementation because real time elapses between the zsh call and the Python call. This script
    does NOT pin the clock (no vendored `date`/`libfaketime`); instead it NORMALIZES every relative-
    time token (`Nm ago`, `Nh ago`, `Nd ago`, `just now`, `yesterday`, and the `Nh Nm` cortex
    countdown shape) to a fixed placeholder before diffing. This is a textual approximation, not a
    proof of numeric equality -- a bucket-boundary flip (e.g. zsh runs at 59m59s, Python runs one
    second later at 1h00m00s) would still show as a false UNEXPECTED diff. None have been observed
    in practice; if one appears, check whether it is a boundary flip before treating it as a port
    bug.

USAGE
-----
    bin/link-parity-harness                    # both render + primitive differentials, real registry
    bin/link-parity-harness render              # only the four-mode whole-command differential
    bin/link-parity-harness primitives          # only the primitive-level differentials
    bin/link-parity-harness render --registry PATH   # use a fixture registry instead of the real one
    bin/link-parity-harness --oracle-ref REF    # override the zsh oracle commit (default: ad99612)
    bin/link-parity-harness --help

Exit code 0: every project/mode identical or fully explained by the three expected deviations.
Exit code 1: at least one UNEXPECTED difference was found (see stdout for the diff).
Exit code 2: setup failure (oracle extraction, missing renderers, missing registry, etc).

`BORG_UPDATE_GOLDEN` is READ NOWHERE in this script. It is not a golden-file tool; it is a live
differential against two running implementations, and it must never be run in any mode that writes
to the owner's real `~/.config/borg/registry.json`.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import difflib
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
from pathlib import Path

ORACLE_REF_DEFAULT = "ad99612"
REQUIRED_ORACLE_FUNCTIONS = ("_borg_link_porcelain", "_borg_link_overview", "_borg_link_deep")
MAX_SETUP_RETRIES = 3

ANSI_RE = re.compile(r"\x1b\[[0-9;]*m")
REL_TIME_RE = re.compile(r"\b\d+[mhd] ago\b|\bjust now\b|\byesterday\b")
COUNTDOWN_RE = re.compile(r"\b\d+h \d+m\b")
PROGRESS_TWO_LINE_RE = re.compile(r"(Progress:[^\n]*?)0\n(\d+)/(\d+) criteria met")
SHIPPED_FIELD_SHIFT_RE = re.compile(r"- \[\] (.+?) \(([^()\n]+)\)")
SHIPPED_EMPTY_PARENS_RE = re.compile(r"(- [^\n]+?) \(\)")


def strip_ansi(text: str) -> str:
    return ANSI_RE.sub("", text)


def _run(cmd: list[str], **kwargs) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    return subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, check=False, **kwargs)


def _retry(label: str, fn):
    """Bounded retry per the harness's own termination rule: at most MAX_SETUP_RETRIES attempts."""
    last_err = None
    for attempt in range(1, MAX_SETUP_RETRIES + 1):
        try:
            return fn()
        except Exception as exc:  # pylint: disable=broad-except
            last_err = exc
            print(f"link-parity-harness: {label} attempt {attempt}/{MAX_SETUP_RETRIES} failed: {exc}",
                  file=sys.stderr)
    print(f"link-parity-harness: STOP -- {label} failed {MAX_SETUP_RETRIES} times, not looping further.",
          file=sys.stderr)
    print(f"link-parity-harness: last error: {last_err}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(2)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Oracle extraction
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def extract_oracle(repo_root: Path, oracle_ref: str, dest: Path) -> Path:
    def _do():
        dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        archive = _run(["git", "-C", str(repo_root), "archive", oracle_ref])
        if archive.returncode != 0:
            raise RuntimeError(f"git archive {oracle_ref} failed: {archive.stderr.strip()}")
        tar = subprocess.run(["tar", "-x", "-C", str(dest)], input=archive.stdout, text=True,
                              capture_output=True, check=False)
        if tar.returncode != 0:
            raise RuntimeError(f"tar extraction failed: {tar.stderr.strip()}")
        return dest

    oracle_dir = _retry(f"extracting oracle tree {oracle_ref}", _do)
    borg_zsh = oracle_dir / "borg.zsh"
    if not borg_zsh.exists():
        print(f"link-parity-harness: STOP -- {borg_zsh} does not exist after extraction", file=sys.stderr)
        sys.exit(2)
    borg_zsh.chmod(0o755)
    text = borg_zsh.read_text()
    missing = [fn for fn in REQUIRED_ORACLE_FUNCTIONS if not re.search(rf"^{re.escape(fn)}\(\)", text, re.M)]
    if missing:
        print(
            f"link-parity-harness: STOP -- oracle ref {oracle_ref} is missing renderer(s) {missing}; "
            "it is not the pre-Phase-3 tree. The zsh oracle only exists at ad99612 in git history -- "
            "if this ref moved, find the commit immediately before the Phase 3 render flip (eb81eab).",
            file=sys.stderr,
        )
        sys.exit(2)
    return oracle_dir


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Sandbox
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

class Sandbox:
    """Owns a throwaway XDG_CONFIG_HOME so borg.zsh's BORG_DIR/BORG_REGISTRY never resolve to the
    real ~/.config/borg. The registry snapshot is re-copied fresh before every invocation (see
    module docstring) so a real side effect (borg_desktop_scan's registry merge) on one run can
    never bleed into the next."""

    def __init__(self, registry_source: Path):
        self.root = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="link-parity-sandbox-"))
        self.config_home = self.root / "config"
        self.borg_dir = self.config_home / "borg"
        self.borg_dir.mkdir(parents=True)
        (self.borg_dir / "desktop").mkdir(parents=True)
        self.registry_source = registry_source
        self.reset()

    def reset(self) -> None:
        shutil.copy(self.registry_source, self.borg_dir / "registry.json")
        for stale in self.borg_dir.glob("registry.json.tmp.*"):
            stale.unlink()

    def env(self) -> dict:
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["XDG_CONFIG_HOME"] = str(self.config_home)
        env["BORG_NO_REAP"] = "1"
        env.pop("BORG_REGISTRY", None)
        env.pop("BORG_DIR", None)
        return env

    def cleanup(self) -> None:
        shutil.rmtree(self.root, ignore_errors=True)


def run_link(borg_zsh: Path, args: list[str], sandbox: Sandbox) -> str:
    sandbox.reset()
    proc = _run([str(borg_zsh), "link", *args], cwd=str(borg_zsh.parent), env=sandbox.env())
    return proc.stdout


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Normalization + classification
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def normalize_relative_time(text: str) -> str:
    text = REL_TIME_RE.sub("<REL>", text)
    text = COUNTDOWN_RE.sub("<COUNTDOWN>", text)
    return text


def normalize_progress_two_line(text: str) -> tuple[str, bool]:
    """Deviation 2: merge zsh's two-line 'Progress: 0' / '0/N criteria met' artifact into the
    single-line shape Python renders, so a real fix elsewhere doesn't hide behind it."""
    fired = bool(PROGRESS_TWO_LINE_RE.search(text))
    merged = PROGRESS_TWO_LINE_RE.sub(lambda m: f"{m.group(1)}0/{m.group(3)} criteria met", text)
    return merged, fired


def normalize_shipped_field_shift(text: str) -> tuple[str, bool]:
    """Deviation 3 (both shapes): the aggregate overview's IFS-tab-collapse field shift
    ('- [] title (project)' -> '- [project] title', matching Python's corrected render) AND the
    deep dive's plain empty-Shipped-date artifact ('- title ()' -> '- title', since the per-project
    TSV has no project field to shift into and Python's `_ship_date_suffix` omits the parens
    entirely whenever ship_date is empty, in both renderers alike). Same root cause -- an empty
    `Shipped:` line -- two different surface shapes depending on how many TSV fields are present."""
    fired = bool(SHIPPED_FIELD_SHIFT_RE.search(text)) or bool(SHIPPED_EMPTY_PARENS_RE.search(text))
    text = SHIPPED_FIELD_SHIFT_RE.sub(lambda m: f"- [{m.group(2)}] {m.group(1)}", text)
    text = SHIPPED_EMPTY_PARENS_RE.sub(lambda m: m.group(1), text)
    return text, fired


_ASSIMILATED_HEADING = "Recently assimilated:"


def _find_assimilated_blocks(lines: list[str]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:
    """(start, end) line-index ranges of the bullet block directly under each 'Recently
    assimilated:' heading in `lines`."""
    blocks = []
    i = 0
    while i < len(lines):
        if _ASSIMILATED_HEADING in lines[i]:
            j = i + 1
            start = j
            while j < len(lines) and lines[j].strip() != "" and strip_ansi(lines[j]).lstrip().startswith("-"):
                j += 1
            blocks.append((start, j))
            i = j
        else:
            i += 1
    return blocks


def normalize_assimilated_order(zsh_text: str, py_text: str) -> tuple[str, str, bool]:
    """Deviation 1: zsh's per-project `(NOm)` glob shows the oldest 3 assimilated plans; Python
    shows the newest 3. When a project has more than 3 assimilated plans these are genuinely
    DIFFERENT subsets, not just a reordering of the same 3 -- so this collapses each paired
    'Recently assimilated:' block to a placeholder on BOTH sides (rather than sorting, which only
    catches a same-set reorder) and reports whether the two blocks actually differed. Blocks are
    paired positionally: both sides render the same number of these headings, in the same order,
    for a given mode/project, since only the RENDERING differs between the two implementations."""
    zsh_lines = zsh_text.split("\n")
    py_lines = py_text.split("\n")
    zsh_blocks = _find_assimilated_blocks(zsh_lines)
    py_blocks = _find_assimilated_blocks(py_lines)
    fired = False
    for (zs, ze), (ps, pe) in zip(zsh_blocks, py_blocks):
        if zsh_lines[zs:ze] != py_lines[ps:pe]:
            fired = True
    # Replace back-to-front so earlier indices in the same list stay valid after a splice.
    for zs, ze in reversed(zsh_blocks):
        zsh_lines[zs:ze] = ["<ASSIMILATED-BLOCK>"]
    for ps, pe in reversed(py_blocks):
        py_lines[ps:pe] = ["<ASSIMILATED-BLOCK>"]
    return "\n".join(zsh_lines), "\n".join(py_lines), fired


def classify(zsh_raw: str, py_raw: str) -> dict:
    """Compare one (zsh, python) output pair. Returns a dict describing the verdict."""
    if zsh_raw == py_raw:
        return {"verdict": "IDENTICAL", "deviations": [], "diff": ""}

    zsh_norm = normalize_relative_time(zsh_raw)
    py_norm = normalize_relative_time(py_raw)

    zsh_norm, dev2 = normalize_progress_two_line(zsh_norm)
    zsh_norm, dev3 = normalize_shipped_field_shift(zsh_norm)
    zsh_norm, py_norm, dev1 = normalize_assimilated_order(zsh_norm, py_norm)

    fired = []
    if dev1:
        fired.append("NOm-assimilated-ordering")
    if dev2:
        fired.append("progress-two-line")
    if dev3:
        fired.append("shipped-field-shift")

    if zsh_norm == py_norm:
        return {"verdict": "EXPECTED", "deviations": fired, "diff": ""}

    diff = "\n".join(
        difflib.unified_diff(
            zsh_norm.split("\n"), py_norm.split("\n"), fromfile="zsh(normalized)", tofile="python(normalized)",
            lineterm="",
        )
    )
    return {"verdict": "UNEXPECTED", "deviations": fired, "diff": diff}


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Render differential
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def cmd_render(repo_root: Path, oracle_ref: str, registry_path: Path) -> int:
    tmp = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="link-parity-oracle-"))
    try:
        oracle_dir = extract_oracle(repo_root, oracle_ref, tmp / "oracle")
        oracle_zsh = oracle_dir / "borg.zsh"
        current_zsh = repo_root / "borg.zsh"
        if not current_zsh.exists():
            print(f"link-parity-harness: STOP -- {current_zsh} does not exist", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2

        sandbox = Sandbox(registry_path)
        try:
            registry = json.loads(registry_path.read_text())
        except Exception as exc:  # pylint: disable=broad-except
            print(f"link-parity-harness: STOP -- could not parse registry {registry_path}: {exc}",
                  file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
        projects = sorted((registry.get("projects") or {}).keys())
        if not projects:
            print(f"link-parity-harness: STOP -- registry {registry_path} has zero projects", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2

        modes: list[tuple[str, list[str]]] = [
            ("overview", []),
            ("porcelain", ["--porcelain"]),
            ("overview --all", ["--all"]),
        ]
        modes.extend(("deep:" + p, [p]) for p in projects)

        results = []
        try:
            for label, args in modes:
                zsh_out = run_link(oracle_zsh, args, sandbox)
                py_out = run_link(current_zsh, args, sandbox)
                verdict = classify(zsh_out, py_out)
                results.append((label, verdict))
        finally:
            sandbox.cleanup()

        identical = [r for r in results if r[1]["verdict"] == "IDENTICAL"]
        expected = [r for r in results if r[1]["verdict"] == "EXPECTED"]
        unexpected = [r for r in results if r[1]["verdict"] == "UNEXPECTED"]

        print(f"link-parity-harness: render differential -- oracle {oracle_ref}, {len(projects)} projects, "
              f"{len(modes)} mode/project cases")
        print(f"  identical:  {len(identical)}")
        print(f"  expected:   {len(expected)}  (matches known deviation(s))")
        print(f"  UNEXPECTED: {len(unexpected)}")
        print()
        for label, verdict in results:
            if verdict["verdict"] == "IDENTICAL":
                continue
            tag = verdict["verdict"]
            devs = ",".join(verdict["deviations"]) or "-"
            print(f"  [{tag}] {label}  deviations={devs}")
            if verdict["verdict"] == "UNEXPECTED":
                print(verdict["diff"])
                print()

        if unexpected:
            print("link-parity-harness: FAIL -- unexpected differences found (see above).", file=sys.stderr)
            return 1
        print("link-parity-harness: PASS -- every difference matches a known, signed-off deviation.")
        return 0
    finally:
        shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Primitive-level differentials
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def _shell_heading_title(path: Path) -> str:
    proc = _run(["bash", "-c", "head -1 \"$1\" | sed 's/^#* *//'", "_", str(path)])
    return proc.stdout.rstrip("\n")


def _shell_ship_date(path: Path) -> str:
    proc = _run(["bash", "-c",
                 "grep -m1 'Shipped:' \"$1\" | sed 's/.*Shipped: *//' | sed 's/ .*//'", "_", str(path)])
    return proc.stdout.rstrip("\n")


def _shell_plan_progress(path: Path) -> tuple[str, str]:
    total = _run(["bash", "-c", "grep -c '^\\- \\[' \"$1\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0", "_", str(path)])
    done = _run(["bash", "-c", "grep -c '^\\- \\[x\\]' \"$1\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0", "_", str(path)])
    return done.stdout.strip(), total.stdout.strip()


def _shell_plan_objective(path: Path) -> str:
    proc = _run(["bash", "-c",
                 "grep -A2 '^## Objective' \"$1\" | grep -v '^## Objective' | grep -v '^$' | head -1",
                 "_", str(path)])
    return proc.stdout.rstrip("\n")


def _py_core(repo_root: Path, func: str, *args: str) -> str:
    code = (
        "import sys, json; sys.path.insert(0, sys.argv[1]); "
        "from borg_core.link import core; "
        f"print(json.dumps(core.{func}(*sys.argv[2:])))"
    )
    proc = _run([sys.executable, "-c", code, str(repo_root), *args])
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        raise RuntimeError(f"core.{func}({args!r}) failed: {proc.stderr.strip()}")
    return json.loads(proc.stdout)


def _collect_sample_files(registry_path: Path, limit: int = 40) -> dict:
    """Real markdown files reachable from the registry: PROJECT_PLAN.md and assimilated plans.
    Read-only -- never written to. Bounded to `limit` per category so this stays fast."""
    registry = json.loads(registry_path.read_text())
    plans: list[Path] = []
    assimilated: list[Path] = []
    for entry in (registry.get("projects") or {}).values():
        path = entry.get("path")
        if not path or path == "null":
            continue
        base = Path(path)
        plan = base / "PROJECT_PLAN.md"
        if plan.is_file():
            plans.append(plan)
        assim_dir = base / "docs" / "plans" / "assimilated"
        if assim_dir.is_dir():
            assimilated.extend(sorted(assim_dir.glob("*.md")))
    return {"plans": plans[:limit], "assimilated": assimilated[:limit]}


def cmd_primitives(repo_root: Path, registry_path: Path) -> int:
    samples = _collect_sample_files(registry_path)
    cases = []

    for path in samples["plans"]:
        text = path.read_text(errors="replace")
        py_title = _py_core(repo_root, "heading_title", text)
        sh_title = _shell_heading_title(path)
        cases.append(("heading_title", str(path), py_title, sh_title))

        py_met, py_total = _py_core(repo_root, "plan_progress", text)
        sh_met, sh_total = _shell_plan_progress(path)
        # Deviation 2 at the primitive level: `grep -c ... || echo 0` prints the two-line "0\n0"
        # artifact (see the module docstring) whenever nothing is checked off; core.plan_progress
        # is the deliberate fix, returning a plain int. Expected iff shell's raw output is that
        # two-line "0\n0" shape and Python's int is its second line.
        progress_deviation = sh_met == "0\n0" and str(py_met) == "0"
        cases.append(("plan_progress", str(path), f"{py_met}/{py_total}", f"{sh_met}/{sh_total}",
                      progress_deviation))

        py_obj = _py_core(repo_root, "plan_objective", text)
        sh_obj = _shell_plan_objective(path)
        expected_deviation = sh_obj == "--" and py_obj == ""
        cases.append(("plan_objective", str(path), py_obj, sh_obj, expected_deviation))

    for path in samples["assimilated"]:
        text = path.read_text(errors="replace")
        py_title = _py_core(repo_root, "heading_title", text)
        sh_title = _shell_heading_title(path)
        cases.append(("heading_title", str(path), py_title, sh_title))

        py_ship = _py_core(repo_root, "ship_date", text)
        sh_ship = _shell_ship_date(path)
        expected_deviation = py_ship.startswith("(**") or sh_ship.startswith("(**")
        cases.append(("ship_date", str(path), py_ship, sh_ship, expected_deviation))

    print(f"link-parity-harness: primitive differential -- {len(cases)} cases across "
          f"{len(samples['plans'])} plans + {len(samples['assimilated'])} assimilated files")
    print("  (render._fold_s vs `fold -s` is already covered by "
          "borg_core/link/test_render.py::TestFoldS::test_matches_real_fold_s_binary -- not duplicated here)")
    print()

    mismatches = 0
    for case in cases:
        prim, path, py_val, sh_val = case[0], case[1], case[2], case[3]
        known = case[4] if len(case) > 4 else False
        if py_val == sh_val:
            continue
        if known:
            print(f"  [EXPECTED] {prim} {path}: python={py_val!r} shell={sh_val!r} "
                  "(known deviation, see script header)")
            continue
        mismatches += 1
        print(f"  [UNEXPECTED] {prim} {path}: python={py_val!r} shell={sh_val!r}")

    print()
    if mismatches:
        print(f"link-parity-harness: FAIL -- {mismatches} unexpected primitive mismatch(es).", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    print("link-parity-harness: PASS -- every primitive differential matched or is a known deviation.")
    return 0


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Entry point
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def _default_registry_path() -> Path:
    xdg = os.environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME") or str(Path.home() / ".config")
    return Path(xdg) / "borg" / "registry.json"


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="link-parity-harness",
        description="Differential oracle for the borg link zsh->Python port. See the module "
        "docstring (top of this file) for the three known deviations and sandbox gotchas.",
        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
    )
    parser.add_argument("mode", nargs="?", choices=["render", "primitives", "all"], default="all")
    parser.add_argument("--oracle-ref", default=ORACLE_REF_DEFAULT,
                         help=f"zsh oracle commit (default: {ORACLE_REF_DEFAULT})")
    parser.add_argument("--registry", type=Path, default=None,
                         help="registry.json to use (default: the real registry at "
                         "$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/borg/registry.json / ~/.config/borg/registry.json, "
                         "READ-ONLY -- this script never writes to it)")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)

    repo_root = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
    registry_path = args.registry or _default_registry_path()
    if not registry_path.is_file():
        print(f"link-parity-harness: STOP -- no registry at {registry_path}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    exit_code = 0
    if args.mode in ("render", "all"):
        exit_code = max(exit_code, cmd_render(repo_root, args.oracle_ref, registry_path))
    if args.mode in ("primitives", "all"):
        if args.mode == "all":
            print()
        exit_code = max(exit_code, cmd_primitives(repo_root, registry_path))
    return exit_code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
